# ExcelDiff

A Windows desktop GUI diff tool for Excel / CSV / TSV. Can be used as a Git / Mercurial difftool.
Two products are built from the same source:

- **EME** (priority / benchmark build, `ExcelDiffEDR.GUI.exe`): reads via ExcelDataReader. Fast reading (benchmark on a ~1.8 MB Excel file takes about 28% of EM's time, ~72% faster); development and benchmark testing use EME as the baseline.
- **EM** (fallback build, `ExcelDiff.GUI.exe`): reads via NPOI. Most complete semantics; serves as the fallback for EDR blind spots and as a validation reference.

The two builds are fully isolated (process / assembly / config / display name). The UI defaults to Simplified Chinese and supports Chinese/English switching.

![Demo](media/demo.gif)

![cell diff](media/cell_diff.png)

## Features

- Diff comparison: row-level + cell-level highlighting (`xls` / `xlsx` / `csv` / `tsv`).
- Resident + tray: single instance stays in the background; show / hide / exit.
- Single-instance IPC: a second invocation is routed to the resident instance over a named pipe, avoiding multiple windows.
- No-diff notification window: optional popup when the two files are identical (`NotifyEqual`).
- Window persistence: position / size / column width / row height / font / search history auto-saved.
- External localization: `lang\en-US.json` / `lang\zh-CN.json` (UTF-8).
- External command / file settings / color settings / diff log output.
- Start on boot (`StartOnBoot`).

## System Requirements

- Windows 7 or later
- .NET Framework 4.6.2

## Supported File Types

- `.xls`
- `.xlsx`
- `.csv`
- `.tsv`

## Build & Deploy

Uses `dotnet msbuild` (no standalone MSBuild); the reference-assembly root must be specified.

### EME (priority / benchmark, EDR read) — output `ExcelDiffEDR.GUI.exe`

```
dotnet msbuild ExcelDiff.GUI/ExcelDiff.GUI.csproj /p:Configuration=Release /p:EdrRead=true /p:TargetFrameworkRootPath="D:\ExcelDiff\packages\refs" /p:IncludePackageReferencesDuringMarkupCompilation=false /p:GenerateResourceMSBuildArchitecture=CurrentArchitecture /p:GenerateResourceMSBuildRuntime=CurrentRuntime /t:Build /v:m /nologo
```

### EM (fallback, NPOI read) — output `ExcelDiff.GUI.exe`

Same as above without `/p:EdrRead=true` (default).

### Deploy order & resident restart

1. Build EME → deploy EME.
2. Build EM → deploy EM.
3. **Restart the matching resident process right after every deploy** (kill process → relaunch with `--startup` from the deployed path).

Reason: the resident process starts from the deployed directory and locks the exe; without killing it the exe cannot be overwritten, and the old process keeps running in memory, distorting test results. Note: do not build both variants in one command line (incremental builds delete each other's output); build them step by step.

### One-command verification gate

```
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File verify.ps1
```

All green = both variants compile + 31 NetDiff tests pass + lang↔resx in sync.

## Usage

### From shortcut

![shortcut](media/shortcut.png)

### From command line

```
ExcelDiff.GUI diff [Options]
```

| Option | Description | Type | Default |
|--------|-------------|------|---------|
| `-s` `--src-path` | Source file path. | string | |
| `-d` `--dst-path` | Dest file path. | string | |
| `-c` `--external-cmd` | Activate an external tool for unsupported file types or on exception. | string | |
| `-i` `--immediately-execute-external-cmd` | Execute external cmd without an error dialog. | bool | false |
| `-w` `--wait-external-cmd` | Wait for the external process to finish. | bool | false |
| `-v` `--validate-extension` | Validate extension before opening a file. | bool | false |
| `-e` `--empty-file-name` | Empty file name. | string | |
| `-k` `--keep-file-history` | Do not record recent files. | bool | false |

> Single-instance IPC: if a resident instance is already running, a new command-line invocation is forwarded to it over a named pipe and the caller exits immediately. A resident launched with `--startup` runs hidden in the tray.

### Git difftool

`.gitconfig`

```
[diff]
tool = ExcelDiff

[difftool "ExcelDiff"]
cmd = \"D:/Program Files/ExcelDiffTool/ExcelDiff.GUI.exe\" diff -s \"$LOCAL\" -d \"$REMOTE\" -c WinMerge -i -w -v -k

[alias]
windiff = difftool -g -y -t ExcelDiff
```

### Mercurial difftool

`mercurial.ini`

```
[merge-tools]
exceldiff.executable = D:\Program Files\ExcelDiffTool\ExcelDiff.GUI.exe
exceldiff.diffargs = diff -s $parent1 -d $child -c WinMerge -i -w -v -e empty -k

[tortoisehg]
vdiff = exceldiff
```

> Adjust paths to your actual deployment directory; benchmark comparisons use EME, EM serves as the fallback validation reference.

### Explorer context menu

After installing `ExcelDiff.ShellExtension` (COM shell extension), compare directly from the Explorer right-click menu.

![context menu](media/context.png)

## Register External Command

Specify an external command via the `--external-cmd` command-line argument.

![external command window](media/ext_cmd_win.png)

### Available Variables

| Value | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| `${SRC}` | Source file path |
| `${DST}` | Dest file path |

It can also be executed from within the tool.

![external command](media/ext_cmd.png)

## File Settings / Color Settings

- File settings: specify a row header or a column header for each file.
- Color settings: customize background colors (alternating rows / column header / row header / added / removed / modified / modified row).

![file settings](media/file_settings.png)

![color settings](media/settings.png)

## Shortcut Keys

| Shortcut Key | Description |
|--------------|-------------|
| Ctrl + → | Next modified cell |
| Ctrl + ← | Previous modified cell |
| Ctrl + ↓ | Next modified row |
| Ctrl + ↑ | Previous modified row |
| Ctrl + K | Next added row |
| Ctrl + I | Previous added row |
| Ctrl + L | Next removed row |
| Ctrl + O | Previous removed row |
| Ctrl + F | Search cell |
| F9 | Next match cell |
| F8 | Previous match cell |
| Ctrl + C | Copy selected cells as TSV |
| Ctrl + Shift + C | Copy selected cells as CSV |
| Ctrl + D | Show(Hide) console |
| Ctrl + B | Output selected cells diff as log |

## Output Diff as Log

Press `Ctrl + D` or choose "Output log" from the context menu to output the diff as a log.
The format can be changed in the "diff extraction settings".

![log](media/log.png)

## No-Diff Window & Language Switch

- **No-diff window**: shown when the two files are identical and `NotifyEqual` is enabled. Close it with the top-right "X" or ESC (closes only the dialog); the red "Exit" button (triggered by Enter) also closes the comparison window.
- **Language switch**: after switching the language in settings, the app closes to apply the change; the next diff command recreates the window with the new language.

## Settings & Persistence

Settings are saved as YAML at:

```
%APPDATA%\<assembly name>\<assembly name>.yml
```

- EME: `%APPDATA%\ExcelDiffEDR.GUI\`
- EM: `%APPDATA%\ExcelDiff.GUI\`

## Regression Verification

- `verify.ps1`: one-command gate (both variants compile + 31 NetDiff tests + lang↔resx sync).
- `DiffHarness\`: headless diff comparison (deterministic diff text of EM/EME outputs).
- `NetDiff\NetDiff.TestRunner\`: offline algorithm unit-test runner.

## Known Problems

- If there are column deletions or additions, they may not be displayed at the expected position. Specify an appropriate header and re-extract the diff:
  1. Select the appropriate header cell.
  2. Right-click to show the context menu.
  3. Choose "Extract diff with this row as header".

